1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,099
Do these five things in Japan.

2
00:00:02,449 --> 00:00:03,552
Do carry some cash.

3
00:00:03,572 --> 00:00:07,571
Cashless payments reached fifty-eight
percent in twenty twenty-five,

4
00:00:07,591 --> 00:00:10,369
so many small shops still want coins and
bills.

5
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:11,997
Do ride the Shinkansen.

6
00:00:12,017 --> 00:00:14,987
The Tokaido line averaged only one point
four minutes

7
00:00:15,007 --> 00:00:18,843
of delay per train in fiscal twenty
twenty-four, disasters included.

8
00:00:19,193 --> 00:00:21,443
Do wash before you soak in an onsen.

9
00:00:21,463 --> 00:00:26,128
The bath is shared, so you scrub first,
and only then step into the water.

10
00:00:26,478 --> 00:00:28,022
Do chase the cherry blossoms.

11
00:00:28,042 --> 00:00:31,365
Tokyo's season began on March nineteenth
in twenty twenty-six,

12
00:00:31,385 --> 00:00:34,459
and the bloom reaches Sapporo more than
five weeks later.

13
00:00:34,809 --> 00:00:36,945
Do reserve before you climb Mount Fuji.

14
00:00:36,965 --> 00:00:39,598
The Yoshida trail season runs from July
first to

15
00:00:39,618 --> 00:00:42,382
September tenth, and the fee is four
thousand yen.

